// Pathfinder 2E visual effects library: the fantasy looks this system's effects have, composed from the engine's
// genre-neutral primitives (engine/fx/fx.js). Part of the system configuration (PF2E_SYSTEM.effects). Data only:
// an adventure pack can add or restyle effects in the same form (its effects.json). Docs: docs/design/board.md
// section 7 (visual effects).
//
// The previous board's ~100 effects, reworked: names say what happens (no character or dungeon-level names);
// effects that were one character's (Chuck's finisher, Kerra's charge, Pip's spells, Jix's songs) and the per-level
// monster sets fold into these, recoloured with a play's colour where needed. Groups: Weapon strikes, Ranged,
// Spell projectiles, Areas, Healing and buffs, Conditions and social, Creature attacks, Movement.
//
// A step: {p: primitive, at|from|to: 'a'|'b'|'b0'|'mid', colour, size/radius/r0/r1/length/speed (squares), ms,
// after (ms), repeat ('n' = the play's count), stagger, vary}. Attacks (attack: true) get the shared hit / crit /
// miss results; impact is when the result shows.

